    "notes": "Fixed/padded signatures. Actual byte length is read by parsing the sign/low-bit fixed region and the unary high-part region; no heuristic zero stripping. HAWK_AVX2 and NTRUGEN_AVX2 explicitly select scalar or upstream SIMD. KeyGen uses integer fixed-point NTRUGEN, signing is integer-based; neither needs floating point or GMP. Native self_test includes SHAKE KATs and 100-case aggregate key/signature hash KATs for degrees 256/512/1024. Expanded-key Sign uses hawk_sign_finish_alt with a decoded key; this API also changes how the RNG is consumed and is additional information, not an isolated decode-only speedup. Timing callback uses the repository SHAKE with an OS seed initialized before measurements."
